## Why This Is Asked
Tests design for multi-tenant ML services with SLA adherence, privacy, and drift handling in a single-region, VPC-bound setup.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoints; per-tenant routing; fair-share scheduling
- QoS, concurrency, canary rollouts; drift detection and retraining cadence
- Data locality, PrivateLink, encryption, audit logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode showing tenant routing
function route(request){
  const tenant = request.tenantId;
  const model = loadTenantModelIfNeeded(tenant);
  return model.predict(request.features);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates ability to design private, language-aware ML inference at scale with strict data locality and per-tenant isolation. Tests routing logic, canary deployment strategies, and cross-language drift handling.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model vs. per-language endpoints
- PrivateLink data residency and IAM isolation
- Canary rollouts and per-language versioning
- Model Registry + Pipelines for safe promotions
- Tenant-scoped storage and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Language route resolver
function routeEndpoint(lang) {
  const map = {
    en: 'ep-en',
    fr: 'ep-fr',
    de: 'ep-de'
  };
  return map[lang] || 'ep-default';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests data residency, tenant isolation, and end-to-end security in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
